# viewtest: the keyboard layout's character of a key (KeyEvent::ch, E2): what a browser names
# the key (KeyboardEvent.key) also when Ctrl or Alt is held and the key types nothing.  "Roh:"
# shows it as =c (=c! a dead key).  keydown / keyup carry the US layout's character; `char "c"`
# plays another layout (here a German keyboard).
click "Rohe Tasten"
click #101
# Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z: the letter with its Shift
key ctrl+z ctrl+shift+z
expect text:"Roh: +C-Z=z -C-Z=z +C-S-Z=Z -C-S-Z=Z" exists
# a German keyboard: Ctrl++ is the key VK_OEM_PLUS ("=" on the US layout), its character "+";
# Ctrl+7 the digit
keydown ctrl left scan 29
keydown + scan 27 char "+"
keyup + scan 27 char "+"
keydown 7 scan 8
keyup 7 scan 8
keyup ctrl left scan 29
expect text:"Roh: +C-Z=z -C-Z=z +C-S-Z=Z -C-S-Z=Z +Strg:L#29 +C-Plus=+#27 -C-Plus=+#27 +C-7=7#8 -C-7=7#8 -Strg:L#29" exists
# a dead key (German ´): its spacing character, marked; keys without a character have none
keydown ] scan 13 char "´" dead
keyup ] scan 13 char "´" dead
keydown f2 char none
keyup f2
key enter
expect text:"Roh: +C-Z=z -C-Z=z +C-S-Z=Z -C-S-Z=Z +Strg:L#29 +C-Plus=+#27 -C-Plus=+#27 +C-7=7#8 -C-7=7#8 -Strg:L#29 +]=´!#13 -]=´!#13 +F2 -F2 +Eingabe -Eingabe" exists
